      "blocks": {
        "q1":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"How much energy does the 230Ah battery store?","answer":"<p>The rated energy is 2,944Wh, calculated from the documented 12.8V and 230Ah ratings. Usable energy depends on system settings, load and operating conditions.</p>"}},
        "q2":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"Can I run a 200A load continuously?","answer":"<p>200A is the documented maximum continuous-discharge rating. The inverter, conductors, fuses, terminals and temperature conditions must also support the planned load.</p>"}},
        "q3":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"What charger size should I use?","answer":"<p>The manual lists 46A as the recommended charge current and 115A as the maximum continuous charge current, using a 14.4V +/- 0.2V CC/CV profile. Coordinate all charging sources within those limits.</p>"}},
        "q4":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"What does IP65 mean for this battery?","answer":"<p>IP65 indicates a dust-tight enclosure with protection against water jets. It is not an immersion rating; keep the battery location, terminals and cable routing protected and follow the installation manual.</p>"}},
        "q5":{"type":"question","settings":{"question":"Where can I review the complete operating limits?","answer":"<p>The current English product manual is available in Documents on this page. Review it together with the charger, inverter and RV manufacturer instructions before installation.</p>"}}
